<title>EL SALVADOR: Salvador's Banco Cuscatlan to place Yankee bond.</title>
<headline>Salvador's Banco Cuscatlan to place Yankee bond.</headline>
<dateline>SAN SALVADOR 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>El Salvadorian bank, Banco Cuscatlan, said on Friday it will place a $50 million five-year Yankee bond, securitized by remittances from El Salvadorians resident in the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes, we are in the sales memorandum stage,&quot; Eduardo Quevedo, director of finance's for the bank, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The flow of money that we capture from Salvadorians will guarantee the issue,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The issue will be led by Daiwa Security, and is the first for Banco Cuscatlan in international capital markets.</p>
<p>((-San Salvador bureau, +503 223-1394))</p>
</text>
